Ahead of the launch of the foldable <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-duo/">iPhone Duo</a>, rumors suggested Apple was focused on <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2025/12/22/iphone-foldable-ultra-thin-glass-crease/">eliminating the crease</a> between the device's two displays. All foldables have a visible crease, and it often becomes easier to see over time from constant folding and unfolding.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/iphone-duo-apps.jpg" alt="" width="1665" height="937" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1063638" /><br/>
On the &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj; product page, one of Apple's FAQs concerns the crease. "Does the inner display of &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj; show a crease where it folds?" reads the question.<br/>
<br/>
Apple's response says the display is "wonderfully flat and smooth," but it doesn't say there's no crease at all and actually skirts the question it asks.<br/>
<blockquote>iPhone Duo features a wonderfully flat and smooth inner display with custom nano-texture finish technology to reduce glare and reflections for an uninterrupted viewing experience. The optically clear adhesives let the display layers glide as the screen folds, minimizing stress and crease.</blockquote><br/>
In the press release for the device, Apple says that the Duo's nano-texture display is meant to minimize the visibility of the crease.<br/>
<blockquote>A premium nano-texture finish reduces glare and reflections, creating a matte surface that minimizes crease visibility and feels great to touch.</blockquote><br/>
Apple does not list a fold cycle count anywhere in its press release or on its website, but it does say the hinge offers "smooth, balanced resistance for long-lasting reliability." Apple also says the hinge has more than 100 components, while the &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj; has support ribs and a titanium panel under the display.<br/>
<br/>
Apple competitor Samsung does list fold cycles for its foldable devices. The new Galaxy Z Fold8, which has the same general shape as the &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj;, is <a href="https://www.sammobile.com/news/galaxy-z-fold-8-how-durable-is-samsung-new-passport-style-foldable-phone/">rated for 500,000 folds</a>.<br/>
<br/>
